Most of that recycled shortlist is not wrong, exactly. It is tired. Mustard, burnt orange, and olive have been the default answer for a decade, repeated so often that nobody stopped to ask whether they still look current or just familiar. Familiar and current are not the same thing, and treating them as interchangeable is how a manicure ends up feeling like an afterthought instead of a choice.

What follows is not another forty-shade scroll. It is a direct answer, broken down by what actually changes your decision: which shades read current versus dated this year, whether matte or glossy suits your plans, and what holds up if you are cooking and hosting all day rather than showing up to someone else's table. By the end, you will know exactly which shade and finish to book or paint, and why it is the right call for your specific Thanksgiving.

