## How to Make Your Thanksgiving Nail Color Last Through the Holiday

Prep matters more than the polish itself. Push back and trim cuticles before applying any base coat, since oil and dead skin at the edges are the single biggest reason a fresh manicure lifts within a day of hosting. A thin base coat, two thin color coats rather than one thick one, and a proper top coat sealed over the free edge of the nail will outlast a rushed application by days.

Gel polish is worth the extra step for anyone hosting, given the water and heat exposure a full day of cooking involves. Regular lacquer works fine for attending, where hands stay drier and the wear is lighter. Either way, the darker <strong>thanksgiving nail colors</strong> from earlier in this guide all benefit from a swipe of cuticle oil the morning of Thanksgiving, which keeps the surrounding skin from looking dry against a dark, glossy shade, exactly where wear tends to show first.

