## The Verdict on This Year's Shade

Burgundy, brown, cranberry, and sage are not a compromise between the eight shades every other guide hands you. They are the four that survived an actual filter: does this still look considered in 2026, or does it just look familiar. Familiar was never the goal.

Pick glossy chocolate brown if the day means hours in the kitchen and you want one shade that works for the whole plan without a second thought. Pick burgundy or cranberry if the table is the main event and the finish can afford to take a little more shine. Skip the flat matte mustard, however many roundups still push it forward. This is not a list to keep scrolling through. It is the shade, chosen, ready to book or paint before the holiday gets any closer.
